dylan: Heads up — I'm proposing a small TF change to the mixed-instance pool to add instance affinity tags + a spot-eviction grace annotation. Goal: reduce cross-region/AZ thrash when we fallback and make interruptions less noisy for the autoscaler. Plan attached below.
anya: Can you paste the diff/plan? worried about unintended replacement of launch templates or ASG churn.
infra-bot: terraform plan: 1 to add, 2 to change, 0 to destroy
kevin: +1 for affinity tags. If we can avoid replacing LT IDs that's ideal. Also we should ensure `create_before_destroy` for the autoscaling_group to avoid transient capacity loss.
 dylan: here's the snippet i'm proposing (pseudo-TF):
```
resource "aws_launch_template" "gpu_spot" {
  name_prefix = "rdw-gpu-spot-"
  image_id    = var.gpu_ami
  instance_type = var.preferred_instance
  tag_specifications = [{
    resource_type = "instance"
    tags = {
      "rr:instance-affinity" = var.affinity_group
      "rdw:spot-fallback" = "true"
    }
  }]
  metadata_options { http_tokens = "required" }
}

resource "aws_autoscaling_group" "gpu_mixed" {
  mixed_instances_policy {
    launch_template { launch_template_specification { id = aws_launch_template.gpu_spot.id }
    }
    instances_distribution { on_demand_percentage_above_base_capacity = 20 }
  }
  lifecycle { create_before_destroy = true }
}
```

asha: We should also add a node-label / instance tag consumed by kube-scheduler so pods can prefer "affinity=stable" nodes. That will make churn tolerant.
kevin: For interruption handling: add the graceful window via the node agent + tag to reduce preemptible eviction storm. E.g., add tag `rdw:spot-grace=120` (seconds) and have the termination-handler use it. That avoids racing when ASG scales.
anya: Is the AMI compatible? we recently rolled kernel + NV driver updates; older AMIs might not honor the spot-terminate hook properly.
 dylan: Good catch — I'll gate the rollout until image pipeline outputs the new AMI. Proposal for rollout: canary in us-west-2a with 10% of GPU capacity for 24h, monitor evictions/billing. If eviction rate drops or stable, expand to whole region, then prod.
infra-bot: running dry-run plan: will change 2 LTs -> adding tags, add 1 ASG config change -> add lifecycle rule
 sasha: Also suggest using instance-weight tweaks in mixed_instances_policy to bias toward cheaper GPUs but keep a minimal reserve of high-throughput instances. e.g., weight p4d=10, g5=4. That, plus affinity tags, should reduce cross-AZ bouncing when certain instance families are evicted.
kevin: policy note — add terraform comment and a sentinel check in CI: no LT replacements without approval. I don't want surprise churn in a mass apply.
anya: +1 to manual approval gate for full rollout. Can we add a feature-flag in TF var to flip canary on/off? That way we can test policy change safely.
 dylan: yep will add `var.canary_percent` and `var.canary_region` and a simple map so default is 0. I'll open a PR with the TF plan and a screenshot of the dry-run. Targeting rollout window Wed 03:00-07:00 UTC to hit low traffic.
infra-bot: Note: remember to tag new LTs with `rdw:owner=eng-infra` and `rdw:ci-build=<pipeline-id>` for future AMI rotation traces.
kevin: one more ops ask — add cloudwatch metric filter for ASG instance replacement count and a short-term alarm for >5 replacements/15m in region to auto-halt the rollout.
 dylan: will add alarms and a manual rollback runbook. Thanks all — I'll post the PR and tag ops leads for approval. :thumbsup:
